 "inference": [
  "The damage of fire is in these stage lists, not in a blast object. The integer is the candidate for the damage amount and the float for a time, because the integers fall as the floats rise in the grenade's list (15 at 2.5, 10 at 7, 5 at 10) and the grenade's projectile lives 10 s. The names are hashes, so this reading is a candidate, not a recorded meaning.",
  "Under that reading the incendiary grenade's fire weakens with its age: 15 per step until 2.5 s, 10 until 7 s, 5 until 10 s. Whether a step is the 0.1 interval or one second is not shown; 15 every 0.1 s would kill in under a second, so per second is the likelier unit.",
  "The thermobaric list (8 / 2, 5 / 1.5) does not rise in its float, so there the float reads as a duration. The two readings cannot both hold; the field's meaning stays open.",
  "The exit affector (3 / 1, interval 0.2) fits the burn that continues after leaving the fire; the registry's 'Fire damage duration' 2.5 is a separate row.",
  "Open vehicle seats have their own list (8 / 2, 6 / 3.5, 4 / 5), lower than on foot."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "Units and meaning of the stage integer and float. Test: stand in a fresh incendiary grenade fire and read health lost over the first second and over the eighth second (15 and 5 expected if the integer is damage per second and the float the fire's age).",
  "Which affector the fire damage rank rows select."
 ],
